<title>USA: Applied Signal Technology wins contract.</title>
<headline>Applied Signal Technology wins contract.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Applied Signal Technology Inc on Monday said it has won an $8.3 million contract, marking the second largest contract in its history.</p>
<p>The contract from Sanders, a Lockheed Martin Corp company, calls for Applied Signal to participate in the Joint SIGINT Avionics Family Lowband Subsystem project.</p>
<p>Applied Signal, a maker of digital signal processing equipment for telecommunications, will be part of a team that designs and builds four Lowband Subsystem Demonstration Units to meet the new Joint Airborne SIGINT Architecture standards.</p>
</text>
